{{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" -}}
# Host {{ .chezmoi.hostname }} (macOS) — runtimes, packages
{{- else -}}
# Host {{ .chezmoi.hostname }} (Arch {{ if eq (.profile | lower) "omarchy" }}desktop{{ else }}server{{ end }}) — runtimes, packages, sudo
{{- end }}

- Runtimes via mise (`mise use -g <tool>`): node, python, uv, on-demand pnpm/bun.
  Neovim via bob. NEVER install node tooling or editors via {{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" }}homebrew — homebrew's{{ else }}pacman — pacman's{{ end }}
  node/npm/pnpm/bun/neovim/vim were deliberately removed. (claude-code is a native
  install, not the {{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" }}homebrew{{ else }}pacman{{ end }} package.)
- Run `mise trust <dir>` after creating a new folder/worktree that carries env config.
{{ if eq (.profile | lower) "mac" -}}
- Packages are tracked in chezmoi under `packages/mac/`. After installing/removing, refresh
  the list and commit so it stays reproducible.
{{- else -}}
- Packages are tracked in chezmoi and sync themselves: the playbook installs a pacman
  `PostTransaction` hook that runs `scripts/sync-package-lists.sh` after any install/remove,
  regenerating this profile's lists under `packages/{{ .profile | lower }}/` and committing them.
  Manual regeneration is normally unnecessary; if you must, run
  `~/.local/share/chezmoi/scripts/{{ if eq (.profile | lower) "server" }}update_server_package_lists.sh{{ else }}update_package_lists.sh{{ end }}`.
- Avoid commands that trigger interactive `sudo` prompts unless asked.
{{- end }}
